# Ten Florals Stock-Basis Repair and CF-01 Admission V2

## Actual defect fixed

The V1 portfolio contained a real stock-lineage parser defect.

Ten diluted working stocks were recorded with:

- `stock_fraction = 1.0`
- `stock_fraction_basis = neat/as supplied`
- `carrier = null`

even though their selected V5 stocks were explicitly 1%, 10%, 20%, 30%, 33%, or 40%.

The defect affected **32 formula-row uses**.

The repaired materials are:

- Ambrofix 30%
- Ambrofix 40%
- Ambrox Super 33%
- Labdanum 10%
- Tonalide 10%
- Blackcurrant Absolute 10%
- cis-3-Hexenol 1%
- Undecavertol 1%
- Bourgeonal 20% in TEC
- Adoxal 10% in DPG

Formula material identities, design shares, phases, functions, formula totals, and formula
hashes were not changed.

## Portfolio closure achieved

After the overlay:

- 545/545 rows have a known stock fraction and fraction basis;
- 520/545 rows have complete carrier identity;
- 25 row uses preserve a carrier-lineage HOLD because V5 states the strength but not the carrier;
- 10/10 formula-definition receipts were generated;
- planned computational active-equivalent arithmetic is available for all non-product-basis rows;
- physical FormulaDoseReceipts remain at 0 because every row still lacks a physical ExactStockRef.

The formula-definition receipt and stock-lineage receipt are now separate immutable objects.

